This is a cool little game. It's impressive that you have a complete system with graphics, sound, physics, geo-mod, etc.<br><br>We had a balancing puzzle in TR too. I love these sorts of physics puzzles in games. With some commercial physics engines these puzzles would be difficult because they don't provide access to the reaction forces.<br><br>If I was going add one more feature it would be collision sounds. They add so much to the physics.<br><br>Do you use a single dynamic BSP for collision? Is it a triangle soup or a collection of convex volumes?<br><br>Please make more games! <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":)" title="Smile"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Sat Oct 20, 2007 4:58 am</p><hr />
